# No Bluetooth input device may power off, suspend or hibernate the unit.
#
# 70-power-switch.rules tags every input device with keys as a logind "system
# button", so logind acts on its KEY_POWER / KEY_SLEEP. The BT remote's HID
# descriptor is a generic Apple keyboard that advertises both, and BlueZ's AVRCP
# uinput device maps a sender's Power command to KEY_POWER. Removing the tag
# keeps their keys flowing to evdev readers (the backend's remote) and keeps the
# Pi 5's own power button, which is not on the Bluetooth bus.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ENV{ID_BUS}=="bluetooth", TAG-="power-switch"
